{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Used this turn to close the one necessary gap I had flagged in my own account rather than leave it standing. The core question's account had recorded as unexplained that the three-node case produced four Accepted messages and `after_drop` still showed an Accepted crossing the wire while the leader did not decide. That is my probe's counter semantics plus the layer's own traffic, and the corrected account says so: a three-node run produces two Accepted messages during the prepare phase because handle_acceptsync pushes one carrying accepted_idx 0 for each synced follower (follower.rs:53-79), then one reply per follower to the entry's AcceptDecide — produced Accepted:4; the two replies are the ones dropped (dropped Accepted:2), and `after_drop` counts messages produced after the first drop, which is why it shows the second follower's reply — that reply was dropped too, so no Accept reached the leader and the non-decision is consistent with the quorum count instead of in tension with it; the two-node case matches (produced Accepted:2, one dropped, heartbeats only after the drop). The flagged limitation is replaced by that explanation, and the measurements, citations and other limits are unchanged. Standing position, all with receipts and scoped limits: the event-backpressure park and cluster stall (capacities 8/64/1024, corrected transport, 21.69s bound, client-side trigger); the core's missing accept-phase repair now measured at both two and three nodes (one dropped receipt at two nodes, two at three, i.e. exactly the quorum's completion, with no protocol traffic beyond heartbeats and the later proposal as the only repair); append_notify's false Ok for an unadopted index with the adopted-vs-unadopted boundary measured; and the actor layer's missing compaction path for the instance it owns, with the panic-to-Shutdown attribution chain and the repository's own compaction documentation as the normative basis.\"}"}}
